@@ -5,7 +5,7 @@
 ### Added
 
 - Added the `retry.accountMode` setting (`sequential` by default, or `balanced`). With `sequential`, Anthropic accounts are used one at a time: every session and subagent follows the account that served last until it is blocked or spent, then moves to the next.
-- New `usage_bar` status-line segment, in the `default` preset right after the context percent (add it to `statusLine.leftSegments` or `rightSegments` in a custom line): a five-cell progress bar and percent for the active account's most constraining usage window, the 5 Hour window by default and the 7 Day window, tagged `7d`, when that is higher. It renders nothing when the provider reports no usage windows.
+- New `usage_bar` status-line segment, in the `default` preset right after the context percent: a five-cell progress bar, the percent used and the window tag (`━━━━━ 100% 7d`) for the active account. New `statusLine.usageWindow` setting (`weekly` by default, `session`, `worst`) chooses the 7 Day window, the 5 Hour window or the more used one. For a Claude model with its own weekly counter (Fable, Mythos, Opus, Sonnet) `weekly` uses the more used of the shared and the model's 7 Day row, tagged `7d fable`; a provider without a 7 Day window falls back to its longest reported window under its own tag. It renders nothing when the provider reports no usage windows, or when several accounts have no resolved one.
 - When a provider holds two or more stored OAuth accounts, the status line names the session's account in the model: `Anthropic (B) > Sonnet 5.5`, and the footer's raw model id reads `anthropic-b/claude-sonnet-5-5`. The letter is the account's position in `omp usage accounts` order (A first) and follows an account change mid-session. Single-account providers look as before.
 - Running background tasks now have their own pinned shelf directly above the Subagents shelf, in the same style: backgrounded `bash` commands, backgrounded `eval` cells and services, each as a row with its id (such as `bg_1099`), a one-line preview of the command and its elapsed time. Jobs that run a subagent stay in the Subagents shelf. `display.pinnedJobs` (`collapsed` by default, `full`, `off`) sets how many rows show before an expander, as `display.pinnedAgents` does for subagents.
 - Name an operator-configured model role such as `@worker` in a task item's `model`, in a mixed-model batch if you like; it resolves to that role's current model and goes through the same `task.perCallModel` gate and approval as an exact `provider/model-id`.
